Ceratopsian Dark for Xfce
========================

The package installs assets for all users. Select the pieces you want in
your own Xfce session.

  Settings > Appearance > Style          Ceratopsian Dark
  Settings > Appearance > Icons          Ceratopsian
  Settings > Window Manager > Style      Ceratopsian-Dark
  Settings > Notifications > Theme        Ceratopsian-Dark
  Settings > Mouse and Touchpad > Theme   Ceratopsian Cursors or Cursors Light

In Desktop Settings, browse to /usr/share/backgrounds/ceratopsian-xfce
for Debian 13 Matte or /usr/share/backgrounds/ceratopsian-variants for
Clean. In Xfce Terminal's Colours preferences, select the Ceratopsian
preset. Administrator-launched GTK apps such as Synaptic can find the
theme in the system directories. Open a new instance to load it.

Optional boot integration on Debian-family systems
--------------------------------------------------

  bash /usr/share/ceratopsian-xfce/extras/boot/install-boot-theme.sh --list

To activate the selected art for GRUB and Plymouth, run the same script
with sudo and add --variant default or --variant clean. The script saves
a backup of the previous boot configuration and regenerates the boot
files. The theme archive's extras guide covers Qt and LightDM.
